---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BuyButton from '../components/BuyButton.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the Author"
  description="Varna Sri Raman wrote and illustrated The Very Last Superhero. Her personal site is idealog.works."
>
  <div class="shell section">
    <header class="page-head stack">
      <p class="eyebrow">Author and illustrator</p>
      <h1>{site.author}</h1>
      <p class="text-muted lede">
        She wrote this book and drew it. Both halves matter here — the illustrations are not
        decoration commissioned afterwards, and the afterword is explicit about it: <em
          >they are not illustrations, they are records</em
        >.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose author stack">
      <h2>Who she is</h2>
      <p>
        Varna Sri Raman is an independent development economist. She works on public policy,
        gender and labour — the economics of unpaid care, budget allocations for informal
        workers, welfare schemes and who they actually reach — and writes about it for
        <a href="https://behanbox.com/author/varna-sri-raman/" rel="noopener">BehanBox</a>,
        <a href="https://thewire.in/author/varna-sri-raman" rel="noopener">The Wire</a> and her
        own <a href="https://policygrounds.press" rel="noopener">PolicyGrounds.press</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        She also runs <a href="https://storywell.in" rel="noopener">StoryWell Books</a>, the
        independent Indian press she started in 2016 and the publisher of this novel. StoryWell
        publishes in English and in regional languages, for readers of every age, and it works
        the way small presses have to work — editing, design and illustration under one roof
        rather than farmed out.
      </p>
      <p>
        The economics and the fiction are not separate careers. This novel is set in 2075 and
        argues about heat, waste, water and who is left carrying the cost of all three; that is
        the same argument, made in a form that lets a fourteen-year-old in Pune pick it up.
      </p>

      <h2>Her other books</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <em>Kalyani's Ant Problem</em> — a children's book written with Papri Sri Raman and
          illustrated by her. StoryWell Books.
        </li>
        <li>
          <em>Happy Lemon</em> — by Papri Sri Raman, illustrated by her. StoryWell Books.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This book</h2>
      <p>
        <em>The Very Last Superhero</em> is a speculative novel set in a climate-collapsed India of
        2075, published by {site.publisher} in {site.edition.toLowerCase()}. It begins after the era
        of superheroes rather than during it, and its argument is that what survives collapse is not
        power but memory — held by ordinary people, animals, salvaged tech and archivists who did
        not stop.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/making">On the Making</a> is her own account of why she wrote it, printed in the
        book and reproduced here in full. It is the best short answer to what the novel is for.
      </p>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        Her personal site is <a href="https://idealog.works" rel="noopener me">idealog.works</a>.
        This site is about the book; that one is about her.
      </p>

      <h2>What is real in it</h2>
      <p>
        The Okhla waste-to-energy plant exists. The heat exists. The book is dedicated in part to
        someone fighting Delhi's waste-to-energy plants, and <a href="/act">How to Help</a> points
        at the people doing that work now.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact">Write to her directly</a> — about the book, a correction, a reader
        submission, or anything on this site that looks wrong.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="buy">
      <BuyButton />
      <p class="text-muted">
        {site.publisher} · {site.edition} · ISBN {site.isbn}
      </p>
    </aside>

    <Newsletter />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .lede,
  .author {
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .author h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .buy {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-l);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .buy p {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
